.TE
.PP
The Windows \f[CR]KERNEL32.DLL\f[R] API is exposed through a single
global structure named \f[CR]KERNEL32\f[R].
.PP
This structure is populated at runtime, so some function pointers may be
\f[CR]NULL\f[R] depending on the target Windows version (especially on
older systems such as Windows 2000).
So, always verify that a function pointer is valid before calling it.
.PP
Available functions are declared in \f[CR]KERNEL32.H\f[R].
You can extend the struct manually if you need additional exports that
are not currently included.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]<CMT/WIN_CORE/KERNEL32.H>\f[R]

int main()
{
    KERNEL32.Sleep(42);
    \f[B]return\f[R] (0);
}
